## Check the implementation

Check that an editorial date is supported by a real review and that a sensor timestamp comes from the owning data source. Test timezone changes, stale data and an absent timestamp.

Use the [civica.uk accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS review dates and freshness](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/review-date) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica.uk markup, Arial typography and civica.uk assets. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

The NHS source explicitly withdraws its old component and directs readers to [helping users know a page is up to date](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/know-that-a-page-is-up-to-date). This page records that replacement, rather than reinstating the retired component.

